###Solving $\triangle AOB$


[[☃ image 1]]

$\begin{align}
&BO=\cos\left(\dfrac{\pi}{3}\right)=\dfrac{1}{2}
\\\\
&AB=\sin\left(\dfrac{\pi}{3}\right)=\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}
\end{align}$

### Relating $\triangle AOB$ back to the unit circle

We now know that $A$ is $\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}$ units ***below*** the $x$-axis and $\dfrac{1}{2}$ units ***to the right*** of the $y$-axis. Therefore, its coordinates are $\left(\dfrac{1}{2},-\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}\right)$.
